{"name":"Sidewalk Grey","hex":"#7b8f99","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sidewalk","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A paved footpath located at the side of a road, for the use of pedestrians.","Any paved footpath, even if not located at the side of a road."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sidewalk"},{"term":"grey","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray.","Synonym of coloured (pertaining to the mixed race of black and white)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grey"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sidewalk","blocks":[{"text":"A sidewalk, pavement or footpath is a footpath along the side of a road or street, designed primarily for pedestrians and low-speed personal transporters such as mobility scooters and postal NEVs. Sidewalks are usually paved by concrete, pavers, bricks, tiles, stones or asphalt, and are normally slightly elevated from the roadway and separated from motor vehicle lanes by a curb or gutter. There may also be a planted strip between the sidewalk and the roadway and between the roadway and the adjacent buildings, land lots and private properties."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Pompei_-_panoramio_%2826%29.jpg/330px-Pompei_-_panoramio_%2826%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sidewalk","wikidata":"Q177749"},{"title":"Grey","blocks":[{"text":"Grey or gray is an intermediate color between black and white. It is a neutral or achromatic color, meaning that it has no chroma. It is the color of a rain or storm cloud, of ash, and of lead."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg/330px-Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link"